<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab-lĭgūrrĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-gurio</span></b> ),
			īvi, ītum, 4, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To lick away</i>, <i>waste</i> or <i>spend in luxurious indulgence</i>: bona, Enn. ap.
			Don. ad <i><span class="en">Ter. Phorm. 2, 2, 25</span></i> (Sat. 29 Vahl.);
				<i><span class="en">Ter.
				Eun. 2, 2, 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patrimonium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 313</span></i>
			 (but in <i><span class="en">Cic. Cat. 2, 5, 10</span></i>, the correct
			read. is <i>obligaverunt</i>).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In mal. part., <i><span class="en">Suet. Gram. 23</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
